# AWS Native Development Rules
# Context engineering rules for AWS Q Developer agentic workflows

## Infrastructure Rules
- Always use AWS Well-Architected Framework principles
- Prefer serverless and managed services over self-managed infrastructure
- Implement defense-in-depth security patterns
- Use AWS native encryption (KMS) for all data at rest and in transit
- Follow least privilege access patterns with IAM roles and policies

## App Runner Specific Rules
- Always deploy App Runner services within VPC for security
- Use VPC connectors for database and internal service connectivity
- Implement auto-scaling based on traffic patterns
- Configure health checks and observability from deployment

## CloudFormation Rules
- Use modular templates with clear separation of concerns
- Implement proper parameter validation and constraints
- Use cross-stack references for shared resources
- Include comprehensive tagging strategy for cost allocation
- Implement proper deletion policies for stateful resources

## Security Rules
- Never hardcode credentials or sensitive data
- Use AWS Secrets Manager for all application secrets
- Implement network isolation with security groups
- Enable encryption for all AWS services that support it
- Use customer-managed KMS keys for enhanced security control

## Operational Rules
- Implement comprehensive logging with CloudWatch
- Use AWS native monitoring and alerting
- Implement automated backup and disaster recovery
- Use Infrastructure as Code for all deployments
- Implement proper environment separation (dev/staging/prod)